# The kernel runs on its own page tables (docs/design.md, "The kernel half"):
# CR3 holds the kernel PML4, CR4 has SMEP, SMAP and PGE, the live tables
# walk as the design says, the direct map reaches .text and .bss, and the
# local APIC answers through the UC device window.
cmdline: test=paging
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: paging: IA32_PAT
expect: now 0x0007040100070406
expect: paging: kernel PML4 at
expect: paging: direct map 4 GiB; 2 MiB pages: 128 WB, 1920 UC
expect: paging: CR3
expect: paging: ok   CR3 holds the kernel PML4
expect: paging: ok   CR4.SMEP, SMAP and PGE are set
expect: paging: ok   the lower half maps nothing
expect: paging: ok   the five guard pages are unmapped
expect: paging: ok   KERNEL_VIRT_BASE is RX, global and supervisor-only
expect: paging: ok   the direct map's alias of .text is read-only and NX
expect: paging: ok   a write through the direct map reaches .bss
expect: paging: ok   the direct map's alias of .text reads the same bytes
expect: paging: ok   the local APIC's window page is UC, RW and NX
expect: paging: ok   the local APIC answers through the device window
expect: TEST PASS
